    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="0578" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg494"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1149.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for the embassy’s use twelve
                    copies of the President’s proclamation of the convention between the United
                    States and Great Britain for the settlement of questions between the two
                    countries with respect to the boundary line between Alaska and the British
                    possessions in North America, signed at Washington on January 24, 1903.</p>
                <p>The President has appointed the Hon. Elihu Root, Secretary of War, Senator Henry
                    Cabot Lodge, of Massachusetts, and ex-Senator George Turner, of Washington, as
                    the American members of the tribunal provided for in the convention.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
